From 4984c2fc654f63ec8647555e4abccff7ac62930c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Haiku 5.5" <a@b>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:23:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rv1126b: Luckfox Aura board, defconfig, and link fixes (5 of
 6)

The Luckfox Aura board, its defconfig, and the link fixes that a defconfig build needed in the
earlier RV1126B files. A clean build of luckfox-aura-rv1126b_defconfig (aarch64, NO_PYTHON=1,
TOOLS_KWBIMAGE and TOOLS_LIBCRYPTO off: no OpenSSL headers on the build machine) gives
spl/u-boot-spl.bin (78027 bytes) and u-boot.bin (630080 bytes), with zero compiler and zero Kconfig
warnings. The binman packaging step is not run: python libfdt (pylibfdt) is not installed here.

Board (board/luckfox/aura-rv1126b, arch/arm/dts/rv1126b-luckfox-aura.dts): console UART2 M0
(the schematic's DEBUG block nets NLUART20TX0M0/RX0M0/CTSN0M0/RTSN0M0); microSD sdmmc0 (SPL pinmux
via rv1126b_sdmmc0_iomux_init); USB3 OTG as a USB2 gadget on usb_drd_dwc3 (generic DWC3, not the seed's
hand-written glue); watchdog on. The board dts includes the SoC node set, then the pin groups, then
the U-Boot overlay (the overlay refers to labels from the first two).

Defconfig (configs/luckfox-aura-rv1126b_defconfig): AArch64; external TPL (ROCKCHIP_EXTERNAL_TPL, the
rkbin DDR blob given as ROCKCHIP_TPL=... on the make line; no TPL built); SPL with DM serial, MMC, pinctrl,
clk, reset, RAM; environment in MMC (ENV_IS_IN_MMC, ENV_REDUNDANT, ENV_SIZE 0x10000, PARTITION_TYPE_GUID,
ENV_MMC_USE_DT, ENV_MMC_DEVICE_INDEX=0, the SD is mmc0 as the board dts's aliases give); hush and saveenv;
fastboot flash mmc; watchdog (WDT, WDT_DW); USB gadget (DWC3 generic, fastboot). BL31 is an input: the
atf-bl31-path binman variable (make BL31=...), not built here. TF-A for RV1126B is not built here.

SoC (patches 1 and 2 files, fixed here): asm/arch/ includes changed to asm/arch-rockchip/ (mainline
path); arch/arm/include/asm/arch-rv1126b/ shims (boot0.h, gpio.h) so the asm/arch link resolves for
SYS_SOC rv1126b; SYS_SOC rv1126b (the idbloader's mkimage -n name, so the rkcommon row matches);
SOC_SPECIFIC_OPTIONS selects HAS_CUSTOM_SYS_INIT_SP_ADDR (as rv1126 does), with CUSTOM_SYS_INIT_SP_ADDR,
SPL_MAX_SIZE (0x80000, seed 16), SPL_LOAD_FIT_ADDRESS, SPL_BSS addresses from the seed header; CFG_IRAM_BASE
0x3ffb0000 (the system SRAM); CFG_SYS_SDRAM_BASE; dram_init from sdram.c (the SoC's own dram_init and
banksize were removed as duplicates); board_init; RAM and DM_RESET enabled; the TPL tiny framework
select removed (it stripped DM for the TPL).

arch_cpu_init (SPL only): two writes that SD boot needs, the sdmmc0 master-secure bit and the non-secure
firewall slaves (seed 426-437). Not ported, with the reason for each in rv1126b.c's comment: the other
master-secure bits, the OTP non-secure setting, the NPU power domain, TSADC trim, USB3 and PERI pipe-PHY
and host-port setup, SARADC IBP, FEPHY pads, FSPI drive levels, and the PVTPLL clock enables.

cpu-info.c: RV1126B reads glb_rst_st from its own CRU struct (the other SoCs are unchanged, behind
#if !defined(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_RV1126B)).

Clock header (fixed here, belongs with patch 4): the reset numbers are in the kernel series' reset header;
the RV1126B_NR_SRST (328) count replaces CLK_NR_SRST in the driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

